// Guards the MIRROR side of the To-Coda/label co-placement, the case the
// post-stack device (2026-08-18, rebuilt session 227) could not cover: ink that
// is NOT the sign stands at the pair's shared barline — here a SEGNO target
// glyph, engraved at the start of the very section the label opens. The pair is
// priced as ONE union extent (OutsideStaffStacker.PlaceMusicMarks +
// MusicMarkEngraver.CoPlaceToCodaWithLabels), so it rides above that ink
// together, sign and label on one line; the old device dropped a raised label
// back to the common rehearsal line, into the very ink the stacker had cleared,
// because behind the stack "raised" and "raised by the sign" looked alike.
// (⚠️ The form deliberately has NO `||` at the boundary: a form-level `||`
// trips a pre-existing collect-resume address drift — `A B || C` alone
// reproduces it, `A B C` does not. That defect is recorded in HANDOFF §1
// session 227; this book guards engraving geometry only.)
title "To Coda beside a segno target"
time 4/4

part m { clef treble }

section A {
  m { c4 d e f | }
}
section B {
  m { g4 a b c' | }
}
section C {
  m { segno e4 d c d | e1 | }
}

form main { A B to coda C }

score main "tocoda-label-mirror" { staff m }
